    "Scouting Notes": "Been nice to see the power come along after the month long stretch with no XBH. \n I do think that the power has ticked up, and in a legitimate way.\n He's now posting exit velo's up to 110+ MPH, which completely changes how I look at his profile.\n Now see a guy who can be a legitimate top of the order bat.\n Baserunning appears to be very good and he's been a very successful base stealer in 2022.\n I actually think I’m lower on his glove than most, I don't think it's plus (see updated note below)\n UPDATED 8/22/22: After watching him play much more often, I do think the glove is plus if he's not at short. I may have been catching him on a few bad days in the past, but I think he's more 2B than SS\n Brewers have been moving him around a bit more so that he has the versatility for the big league level. \n Overall, he’s probably ready for a shot in the majors right now and I think he will be a solid starter at his most likely outcome. His ceiling is a fringe all star if the thump in the bat is legitimate.",
